Description:
  Installs Solid Errors with HTTP authentication and engine mounting.

  Generates an initializer, adds routes, creates a BackstageController,
  and runs the solid_errors:install generator.

  Authentication tries Rails credentials (backstage.username/password)
  first, then falls back to environment variables.
  With Clave installed, the backstage is behind the app's sign-in instead:
  users listed under backstage.emails in credentials get in, anyone else
  gets a 404, and the Basic Auth is taken out of the files it wrote.

  Regardless of options, ApplicationJob is patched to tag reported errors
  with the job class, arguments, and id, so background-job failures appear
  in the Solid Errors dashboard with replayable context.

  With --agent, it also generates read-only AI-agent triage tooling: query
  and triage objects over the errors store (with a redaction pass), a
  bin/failures runner, and a stdio MCP server (bin/failures-mcp, gem "mcp").
  The agent tooling never writes — resolution stays in the dashboards.

  When maquina:mcp is installed (app/models/mcp/tools.rb exists), it also
  writes app/models/mcp/tools/solid_errors.rb: the read-only MCP tools
  list_failures, get_failure and top_exceptions, visible only to users on the
  backstage list (User#backstage_access?) through the OAuth-backed /mcp server.
  With --mcp-write the file also gets resolve_failure, a write tool that needs
  a token with the write scope; an existing tool file is never overwritten. They call FailureTriage, so
  app/agents/{error_redactor,errors_query,failure_triage}.rb are copied when
  missing, even without --agent. Without maquina:mcp nothing MCP-related is
  written; running maquina:mcp later installs the same tools.

  To query a deployed app over stdio instead, run the stdio server where the
  errors DB lives and tunnel its stdio (the post-install prints ssh/docker/kamal
  examples), or copy storage/<env>_errors.sqlite3 down for offline analysis.

Examples:
  rails g maquina:solid_errors --prefix /admin

  rails g maquina:solid_errors --prefix /backstage \
    --user-env-var ADMIN_USER \
    --password-env-var ADMIN_PASSWORD

  rails g maquina:solid_errors --prefix /admin --agent

  rails g maquina:solid_errors --prefix /admin --mcp-write
